window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["seat-cupra/altea-5p"]={"altea-5p-facelift-activate-bluetooth-on-rns-315":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth on the RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Not all RNS-315 are equipped with a Bluetooth module.</strong> </p>\n<figure><table><thead><tr><td>Module compatibility list</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3C0 035 279</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 A</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 B</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 C</td><td>Yes (conditional)</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 D</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 E</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 F</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 G</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 H</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 J</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 K</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>You can also remove the RNS 315 from its slot to check. Behind it, you’ll find a label with the RNS-315’s MAC address.<br/>If the MAC address contains only zeros (MAC: 00:00:00:00:00:00), your RNS-315 is not equipped with the Bluetooth module. </p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns_315_j_mac_non-6328b9e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns315_mac_oui-eed1a386.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>3</strong><br/>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck the “Telephone Transceiver inactive” box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS315_3C0-035-279_Module37_Byte3-74e93c9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-activate-hidden-menu-rns-315":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the hidden menu in RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Developer mode (temporary)</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong><em>Enabled</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS 315.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-035-279_Module37_Adaptation_Developer_mode_tem-59109da4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-activate-hidden-menu-rns-510":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the hidden menu in RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 50</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1T0-035-680-C_Module37_Adaptation_Channel50-1a7d6a90.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rearview camera after it has been installed on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510 (retrofit).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>3</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>6</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) installed/active.”</p>\n<p><strong><strong><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong></strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>0</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>5</strong> to “Rear View Camera installed.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/CA86A611-2F74-4201-B791-7A74BC107A01-1024x482-c9f00e16.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The two pins from the backup camera are used in the 12-pin Quadlock connector (blue).<br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","altea-5p-facelift-activate-rns-510-voice-command":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate voice control on the RNS 510 (SDS).  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:</strong> RNS 510 firmware must be version v2660.</p>\n<p>Activating voice control brings up the “Voice control” menu in the RNS 510’s SETUP menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>3</strong>, check the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Microphone Diagnostics active</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>7</strong>, uncheck the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Voice Control inactive</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS510_Menu_Commande_Vocale-bf5955d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>To install the microphone, connect the microphone lead to the rear of the RNS 510. Connect to pins (Mic-)C1 and (Mic+)C7. </p>","altea-5p-facelift-changing-the-rcd-rns-510-theme":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the display theme of the RCD 510 and RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” for RNS510 and “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” for RCD510.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>4-5</strong>: Select from 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/69C76009-6EC7-465A-A676-8E39BA840A6B-6689b9e0.webp\"/><figcaption>Highline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3A58F148-9FBB-4DD8-BF05-E03A5351E3A8-e9b6cb9b.webp\"/><figcaption>Sportsline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4894A3B7-2ED2-4A75-9D46-CA3BFCF5A76C-8fb8de15.webp\"/><figcaption>Premium</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD / RNS 510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","altea-5p-facelift-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Cliquer sur « <strong>Codage – 07</strong> » puis cliquer sur « <strong>Assistant Codage Long</strong>« .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>: “<br/>” Then uncheck bit <strong>0: </strong> <strong>“Brakepad warning active/installed”</strong> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-lock-the-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-the-rns-510":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the RNS 510’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 43</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(CD/DVD Ejection Lock active)</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-lowering-the-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>09 – Centrale Elec</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf61-d4a12d4d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf62-a22a3a65.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte<strong> 4</strong> and check bit <strong>3 “</strong> <strong>Mirror Lowering With Reverse Rear </strong>” to activate mirror lowering when shifting into reverse gear:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf63-d65eea5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– After this operation, click on the “Output” menu, then validate “OK”.  </p>\n<p>A message appears to inform you that the coding has been accepted.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on<strong> “Select” </strong>, then click on<strong> “52 – Passenger door”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>256</strong> to the value</em></p>","altea-5p-facelift-needle-check":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates needle sweep when vehicle is started. (Needle Sweep)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-ops-speed-camera-display-on-car-radio-screen":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the display of OPS speed cameras on the car radio screen.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>Please note: The vehicle must be equipped with a compatible car radio (RCD-310, RCD-510, RNS-315, RNS-510).</em></strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Optical illustration active”.</em></p>","altea-5p-facelift-programming-a-remote-control":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.<br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Ignition Authorization)</strong>, you cannot program a new remote control using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the process.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>7 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 7 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong>“Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/programmertelecommande-51bf4068.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-remove-alarm-belt":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>1: </strong>“<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-resetting-the-remote-controls":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle. </p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong><br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Start Authorization)</strong>, you cannot delete the remote controls using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-facelift-speed-limit-display-rns-510":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Seat Altea 5P facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/seat_altea_5p_facelift-70676c2d.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS 510 navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”. Then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong><br/>Activate Bit <strong>2</strong>: Speed Threshold for Destination Input active</p>\n<p>+ use voice command to activate Bit 3: Speed Threshold for Speech Destination Input active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510speed-9dcbaa67.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-activate-driving-school-mode-rcd-210-rcd-310":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to add a Driving School mode view to the RCD 210, RCD 310 that displays turn signals, speed … (Also ideal for accompanied driving) <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“56 – Radio</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Channel 2</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“1</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6_golf_vi_fahrschulfunktion-5b883ac1.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-activate-leaving-home-without-light-sensor":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: automatically switches on the headlights each time the vehicle is unlocked.  </p>\n<p>The headlights will come on whether it’s day or night. They stay on for about 30 sec.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click ” <strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then “Long Coding Helper”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Driving Light Assistance When Leaving Home active”</em></p>","altea-5p-activate-mood-lighting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate ambient lighting. (After installation of wiring and lighting for retrofitting)  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 Ambient lighting activation. 1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>20</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Footwell Lights installed”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 Ambient lighting setting :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Channel <strong>27</strong> “Footwell Lighting Dimming (with open Door)”.</p>\n<p><em>Set a value between 0 and 200 (for 100% lighting, set 200).</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 Activate ambient lighting while driving :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Footwell Lights withbTerminal 58d active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 4 Ambient lighting control while driving :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Channel<strong> 35</strong> “Footwell Lighting Dimming (with Terminal 58d)”.</p>\n<p><em>Set a value between 0 and 200 (for 100% lighting, set 200).</em></p>","altea-5p-activate-turn-signals-in-us-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate US indicators. (Altea phase 1 only)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>Byte 7</strong>: Enter value<strong> 32</strong> in <strong>Dec</strong> box<br/>(value in % of intensity, origin: 0)</p>\n<p>Decimal examples shown in yellow in the image:<br/>14 (corresponds to a 20% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>1E (corresponds to a 30% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>28 (corresponds to a 40% variation in the indicator lights)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-937-049-Q_Module09_Byte7-16502f21.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-adjusting-the-power-steering-stiffness":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to adjust the power steering stiffness for a smoother or stiffer, sportier steering feel.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>44 – Power Steering” / “44-steering assist.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5 – Select </strong><strong> Channel 1, </strong> then <em>enter a value between<strong> 1</strong> and <strong>15</strong> based on your preferred hardness level</em></p>\n<p><strong>Or Line 2: (If Channel 1 is unavailable)</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>44 – Power Steering” / “44-steering assist.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5 – Choose </strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>xxx1x for smooth steering</li>\n<li>xxx2x for a sporty ride</li>\n<li>xxx3x for a stiff steering feel</li>\n<li>xxx4x for a firmer steering feel</li>\n<li>xxx5x for very stiff steering</li>\n</ul>","altea-5p-ambient-light-intensity":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Used to adjust ambient lighting intensity.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 05</strong> (Footwell Lightning Dimming)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> <strong>–</strong> Select intensity from 20 to 100% (in 1% increments)</p>","altea-5p-automatic-closing-of-windows-and-roof-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Automatically closes the windows and sunroof when it rains. </p>\n<p>The vehicle must be locked using the remote control for this to work. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf561-c90da3e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “2” and click ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf56-9439cbb9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte 0 and check bit 2, <strong>“Rain Closing active</strong>,” to enable the windows and roof to close when it rains:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-5-d61c5dd9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>7 – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu</p>\n<p> Then click “OK”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-7-353fb01b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“46 – Central Conv”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Then click <strong>” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>9</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Closing (0 = nonrecurring / 1 = permanent)” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Uncheck “Comfort Closing via Rain Light Sensor (Rain Closing) inactive” </em> </p>","altea-5p-automatic-door-locks":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres_vw-auto-loc-ce03b1da.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4 : </strong> Check “Auto-Lock (automatic locking from 15 km/h)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door unlocking when the ignition key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Canal 05</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-door-unlock-798a1163.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock (unlocking after removing the key from the ignition)” </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-automatic-headlamp-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-automatic-headlamp-activation-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte<strong> 0</strong> Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-change-odb-language":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Select the language of your on-board computer.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value according to the selected language</em></p>\n<p><em>1 = German</em><br/><em>2 = English</em><br/><em>3 = French</em><br/><em>4 = Italian</em><br/><em>5 = Spanish</em><br/><em>6 = Portuguese</em></p>","altea-5p-comfort-flasher":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate and set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select Byte <strong>2</strong>,  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>1</strong>: check<strong>“Comfort Turn Signal”.</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select<strong>“Comfort Turn Signal”</strong> from the drop-down list</p>\n<p>Choose a value between 1 and 5 for the number of flashes</p>","altea-5p-coming-home-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is locked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01</strong> (Coming-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","altea-5p-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate cornering lights with fog lamps.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible for vehicles with a 30 Byte power plant.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte 23 : </em><br/><em>Bit 2: Check “Internal Turn Light Control Algorithm active”.</em><br/><em>Bit 3-4: Select “08 Turn Lights via fog lights” from the drop-down list</em></p>","altea-5p-defrost-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the operating time for mirror and rear window defrosting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> (Rear Window &amp; Outside Mirror Heater Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>1 to 254 min</strong> (in 1 min increments).</p>","altea-5p-disable-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear windshield wiper during reversing when the front windshield wipers are operating.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 1 :</strong></em><br/><em><strong>Bit 7 </strong>: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper continiously active”.</em></p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 2 : </strong></em><br/><em><strong>Bit 0</strong>: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper intermitent active”.</em></p>","altea-5p-door-lock-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door lock confirmation when using the key.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>Channel 11</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“46 – Module Confort</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4<strong>– </strong> Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1: </strong> Tick “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with beep/horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-door-lock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door lock confirmation when using the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 10</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vagcom-golf5-e5c80be6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3: </strong> Tick “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with Beep/Horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-door-unlock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to set the door unlock confirmation when using the remote control.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 07</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 10</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Tick “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with Beep/Horn)</em></p>","altea-5p-door-unlocking-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door unlock confirmation when using the key.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 08</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>10</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with blinking lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with a beep or horn)</em></p>","altea-5p-fixed-the-obd-fuel-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to correct the fuel consumption display on the onboard computer. </p>\n<p><strong>This setting can only be changed on mid-range and high-end models</strong>. <br/><em>Note: Changes made to this setting affect the display of instantaneous fuel consumption, average fuel consumption, and fuel level.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click <strong> “17 – Instruments.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> <em>“Consumption Correction”</em></p>\n<p><em>Set the consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g., l/100 km): Specified: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9.8 / 9.73 ? 105.38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105 <br/>Example 2: Calculation based on distance per volume (e.g., MPG): Target: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24, and 95.83) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96       </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correction-consommation-odb-d51db18e.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-fold-down-mirrors-with-ignition-off-and-door-open":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Allows mirrors to be folded down even after the ignition has been switched off and a door opened.  </p>\n<p><em>(Also enables windows and sunroof to be closed)</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>6</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Uncheck “Power Windows/Sunroof disabled after door Opening”.</em></p>","altea-5p-headlamp-washer-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to set how long the headlight washers remain activated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong> (Headlight Washer Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select a duration between <strong>50 and 10,000 ms</strong> (in 50-ms increments).</p>","altea-5p-leaving-home-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is unlocked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 02</strong> (Leaving-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","altea-5p-one-touch-window-closure":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate closing and opening of the windows and sunroof with the remote control <strong>WITHOUT </strong>remaining pressed until the windows are completely closed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition turned off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition and launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Central Conv.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click ” <strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then “Long Coding Helper”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> <em>Byte 6: </em><br/><em>Bit 6: Check “Comfort Function Automatic Closing”</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Uncheck “Comfort function power windows/sunroof via remote control inactive”.</li>\n<li>Check “Comfort opening power windows via remote control active”.</li>\n<li>Check “Comfort closing power windows via remote control active”.</li>\n<li>Check “Closing sunroof via remote control active” (sunroof)</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/ComfortConv-byte6-9f2c129f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 17</strong> (Comfort function)</p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0944-1024x741-ec4d5180.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Pressing the remote control’s close button for 3 seconds will first lock the doors and then close the windows, without having to keep the button pressed until they are fully closed</em>.</p>","altea-5p-programming-a-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program the remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the procedure.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>4 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 4 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong> “Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel01-10148edb.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-remove-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> –  <em>The third and fourth coding digits (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to modify Instrument module options. To suppress the belt alarm, subtract <strong>2</strong> from these digits. </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial coding (with belt alarm) is: <strong>0023103</strong></p>\n<p>To delete the belt alarm, simply recode as follows: <strong>0021103 </strong><em>(23 – 02 = 21)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-reset-the-remote-controls":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle.</p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“How to Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Used to set up selective door unlocking. </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 03</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Selective Central Locking (Single Door Opening)” </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","altea-5p-activate-daytime-running-lights-with-fog-lamps-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows fog lights to be used as daytime running lights.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Lights (North America)”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/scandinavie_194-c7df4fa8.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7 – </strong> <em>Byte<strong> 17</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light with dimmed Low Beam” (or “Daytime Running Light via Fog Lights,” depending on your version of VCDS)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/ab_975-e7b60077.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/veilleusejour3-c639151f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>8-</strong> Adjusting the fog light intensity (from 1% to 99%)</p>\n<p><em>Byte 20: </em><br/><em>Change the value in the Dec box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/VagComByte20-adce5646.webp\"/></figure>"};
